# models/ is 780 MB and none of it belongs in a git history.
#
# A file earns a line below by failing one question: can anything in
# this repository rebuild it? Exactly one does. Everything else is the
# output of a generator that is committed here -- cache, previews,
# every printed size of a design that has dials, and every plate off
# the experimental shelf, which differ from today's build only because
# the code moved on. That is an argument for committing the code, which
# is done, not for storing what it printed.
#
# The rest is other people's designs on a public repository, work
# derived from them, and one-off local exports. Git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded, hence the walk down a level.
models/*

# The specimen: a photogrammetry bake of one tooth, read at runtime by
# the stand page, the jig page and gen_tooth_stand. No generator makes
# it and none ever will -- it came off a scanner. Three copies were on
# disk; BigMeherrin was identical to this one vertex for vertex and
# sale145_tooth was the same tooth off another bake.
!models/specimen/
models/specimen/*
!models/specimen/meherrin-textured.glb

*.gcode
.serve.pid
.serve.log
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
tools/index_out/
